(ROOT/'docs/stage8_1_report.md').write_text('# Stage 8.1 report\n\nStage 8.1 SOFTWARE PASS. Hardware NOT TESTED.\n\n| Backend | Result | Tests |\n|---|---|---:|\n'+rows+'\n\nEnvironment: the current user, WSL Ubuntu 26.04, Zephyr v4.4.2, QEMU 10.2.1, Renode 1.17.0 portable, system Python. Full commands/version output: evidence/stage8_1/environment.json. Historical 133/133 rerun passed; historical evidence unchanged. New counts represent independently executed Hello/GPIO/CAN/UART and Renode GPIO/USART/GDB groups, not individual assertions.\n\nQEMU retains original ARM AN385 firmware. native_sim is Linux x86_64 because 32-bit host linker libraries are absent; no multilib installed. GPIO tests 8 outputs, 4 inputs, 1000 switches, 100 rising/falling callbacks and unsupported configuration handling. CAN loops 1000 standard/extended frames with exact ID/DLC/payload checks, plus empty receive and invalid DLC. This does not test physical arbitration. UART uses a real PTY and host process, 101 messages, fragments, incomplete-frame timeout, overlong frame rejection and reconnect by closing/reopening the slave. It does not simulate unplugging a physical cable. Optional vcan is BLOCKED because CAP_NET_ADMIN is absent.\n\nRenode bare-metal STM32F103 firmware boots, writes GPIO patterns and observes model registers, receives PC13 Button through EXTI/NVIC (10 edges), exchanges 20 USART messages with interrupt RX/ring buffering, rejects overlong frames and reports incomplete-frame timeout. GDB checks CPU registers, GPIO/TX/EXTI breakpoints and single stepping. Renode logs show RCC enable registers are unimplemented SVD placeholders; no full clock tree behavior is claimed. Official platform includes broad mapped Flash/SRAM, not real Blue Pill/ZET6 capacity. No bxCAN instance: UNSUPPORTED. ZET6 package wiring and hardware deployability remain unverified.\n\nRenode source URL and archive SHA256 are pinned in simulation/renode/package.lock.json. No external package or source tree is committed. Failed early native config/header/invalid-pin and Renode Button/reset attempts remain in raw logs; only final successful runs determine the result.\n\nBaseline commit: 59ccb09. Delivery commit: see Git log for the Stage 8.1 delivery commit. Architecture and qualified capabilities: stage8_1_architecture.md and stage8_1_peripheral_support.md. Reproduce with python3 scripts/accept_stage8_1.py --backend all (fresh complete regression); individual backend options are also available. Stage 8.2 was not implemented.\n')
